          {
            "uid": "ef1217f9f56bf05fb225871d",
            "title": "An Agentic AI Framework for Autonomous Cross-View Kernel Rootkit Detection and Response in Cloud Environments",
            "url": "https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-10762752/v1",
            "published": "2026-11-13T00:00:00+00:00",
            "summary": "Abstract Kernel-level rootkits subvert the operating system to conceal the network ports through which they maintain covert channels, and cloud tenants who cannot access the hypervisor have few reliable defences. Existing detectors stop at a verdict, leaving investigation and response to human analysts and admitting a window during which an active rootkit persists. This paper presents an agentic AI framework that both detects and autonomously responds to kernel rootkits through port-level behavioural analysis. On cloud guests hosted on Google Cloud Platform, a kernel-mode Port Enumerator and a user-mode Port Monitor produce cross-view port lists whose discrepancy, formalized here as a temporal behavioural signal, is classified by a deep ensemble of CNN-LSTM, Bi-LSTM, Autoencoder and GAN. The resulting Rootkit/Benign verdict is handed to an LLM Agent Orchestrator that executes an autonomous perceive-plan-act-reflect loop, invoking security tools under human-in-the-loop oversight for high-impact actions. A second evidence channel is released with the paper as a labelled concealment matrix of 87 kernel rootkit samples described by a binary vector over a 968-entry dictionary of concealed objects, each carrying the technique it uses to hide. We give a mathematical model of the cross-view signal, the fused decision, and the agent’s utility-driven action selection. Evaluated on a Wind",
            "source": "OpenAlex Inference",
            "kind": "research",
            "doi": "10.21203/rs.3.rs-10762752/v1",
            "date_precision": "day",
            "aliases": [
              "doi:10.21203/rs.3.rs-10762752/v1",
              "url:https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-10762752/v1"
            ]
          }
        ],
